Put the values of every fill of numbers in one passive data segment.

Patches 0008 and 0009 give an array its values in the start function, from a
passive segment of its own, which the start function then drops. A heap of
many strings made as many segments: the module jwonder writes for a Hibernate
program held 116 440, and V8 refuses a module of more than 100 000 data
segments (`kV8MaxWasmDataSegments`).

Once state is applied for the last time, the values of every fill of numbers
go into one segment, in the order of the fills. Each `array.init_data` reads
its values at their offset there, and one `data.drop` follows the last copy.
The values copied and the order of the copies do not change. Element fills
keep a segment each: few arrays hold more references than an
`array.new_fixed` can.

